  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting of a blue and green rocket with pilot faces blasting diagonally over a row of houses, while a child like figure with a globe head watches.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on canvas. A large rocket in blue, green and yellow with two pilot faces in its windows and a red swirl on its nose crosses the upper half diagonally, trailing orange flame. A row of tall narrow houses in olive, orange and red with arched doors stands at lower centre on a curved ground of coloured map tiles. At lower left a small figure in a yellow suit with a striped globe helmet stands beside a large purple striped sphere, with orange flames and a smaller striped ball behind. Striped balls and a ringed sphere float at left. Thick black outlines, strong colour, visible brushwork.",
    "impression": "A launch seen from the ground, with one small figure left behind in a helmet that is also a globe. The title gives it a note of loss: the operators have departed and the little one watches the ship go. It is a space age bedtime story in paint.",
